<title>GHANA: France gives $5 mln to improve Accra's drains.</title>
<headline>France gives $5 mln to improve Accra's drains.</headline>
<dateline>ACCRA 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>France said on Friday it was giving Ghana $5 million to improve the drainage system in the capital, Accra, where rainy season flooding has killed four people this year and caused telecommunications blackouts in the past.</p>
<p>The Caisse Francaise de Developpement, France's overseas aid agency, said in a statement the grant would also help improve hygiene and sanitation in the affected areas.</p>
<p>Details of the project should be finalised by October, allowing work to begin early in 1998.</p>
<p>Accra suffers flooding every year in the rainy season from May to July.</p>
<p>Four deaths have been recorded so far this year and 26 people died in one day in July two years ago, when the rains also knocked out Ghana's telephone system for about a week.</p>
</text>
